  "facts": [
    "The Martwa Wisła Tunnel, nicknamed Damroka, was bored by a 12.6‑metre shield, the largest tunnel boring machine ever used in Poland at the time of its 2013 start.",
    "After a delayed schedule, the tunnel opened to cars on 24 April 2016, replacing the historic Wisłoujście ferry that had crossed the Martwa Wisła since 1977.",
    "Every third Sunday of April, the tunnel closes to vehicles and opens to cyclists, a tradition begun after the tunnel’s 2016 inauguration and honoring its patron, Archbishop Tadeusz Gocłowski."
